@flexiarg contracts/holder-states-the-claim
@title The Holder States Exactly What Correspondence Is Claimed
@keywords holder, transcription, not-live-path, live-shadow, live-enactment, lagging, live-selection
@audience contract emitters, reviewers, readers of certification status
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; holders in mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/MachineContracts.lean and emit-machine-contracts.py HOLDERS)
@references [contracts/declare-the-reductions translation/declare-what-is-preserved hygiene/settle-with-meters]
@see-also pattern-interpretation/route-the-untranslatable
@how each entry carries one holder: model-transcription-only (Lean mirrors legacy code; no correspondence claimed); runtime-correspondence-not-live-path (tested function computes the declaration; not called live); runtime-correspondence-live-shadow (called live, result only recorded); runtime-correspondence-live-enactment (called live and determines enacted output); runtime-correspondence-lagging (correspondence except on a named input class, stated first in the falsifier); runtime-correspondence-live-selection (reserved; refused until its authorising decision). The verifier checks holder-specific requirements (live-call-site; LAGGING prefix) and refuses reserved holders.
@violation-signature a live claim with no resolvable call site; a disagreement between Lean and runtime not declared; a reserved holder emitted early; "lagging" left in place after the runtime caught up.
! conclusion: Every contract entry's holder states which correspondence is claimed, and the verifier enforces what each holder requires.

  + context: Contracts accumulate while the runtime moves from legacy code to aligned, shadowed and finally live implementations.

  + IF:
    An entry records Lean–runtime correspondence.

  + HOWEVER:
    Stages change quickly and one word ("certified") cannot carry them.

  + THEN:
    Choose the holder that states the stage, and let the verifier check it.

  + BECAUSE:
    The holder is what a reader uses to decide whether a proof says anything about the running War Machine.

  + evidence: P10 lag declared (27bfcd3fff) and closed when futon2 8222c700 landed (dd56aa89d8); first live-shadow entry shadow-cascade-g (r9); first live-enactment entry acting-order (r12, 7e6760dba5); live-selection reserved for P11 step 3.
